index 0000000..c54b6bb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/vars/podYaml.md
@@ -0,0 +1,112 @@
+# podYaml
+
+The pod of a declarative pipeline's Kubernetes agent. `podYaml` renders the pod spec as YAML for the
+agent's `yaml`. The pod holds the library sidecars named in `templates:`, then one container for
+each entry of `images:`, in the order given.
+
+```groovy
+agent {
+    kubernetes {
+        inheritFrom 'jenkins-agent'
+        yaml podYaml(templates: ['k8s'], images: ['node:24-bookworm'])
+    }
+}
+
+stages {
+    stage('Test') {
+        steps {
+            container('node') {
+                sh 'npm ci && npm test'
+            }
+        }
+    }
+}
+```
+
+Every container runs `sleep infinity`, so it lives as long as the pod. Every image is pulled with
+`imagePullPolicy: Always`, so an image that floats on a tag such as `:latest` is that tag's current
+image on every build. `container('<name>') { ... }` runs a stage's steps in the container.
+
+## Arguments
+
+`podYaml(templates: [...], images: [...])` takes these two named arguments, both lists and both
+optional. Any other argument fails the build.
+
+### templates
+
+Library sidecars, by name. The container takes the template's name.
+
+| Template               | Image                                                             | What it carries                                                                  |
+| ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `k8s`                  | `registry:5000/k8s:1.35.5`                                        | kubectl, crane                                                                   |
+| `modern-app-toolchain` | `registry:5000/kube-coder-modern-app-toolchain:node-24`, uid 1000 | KubeCoder's full-stack tool image: Node 24 with npm, pnpm and bun, poetry, ruff, uv, git |
+
+`modern-app-toolchain` runs as uid 1000, the agent's own user: git refuses a checkout that another
+uid owns. A template name the library does not have fails the build, and the error lists the ones
+it has.
+
+### images
+
+Every other container, one entry each, in one of two forms.
+
+**A string** is an image reference. The container is named after the image's last path segment,
+without its tag or digest: `node:24-bookworm` runs as `node`, and
+`registry:5000/kube-coder-go-toolchain:latest` as `kube-coder-go-toolchain`.
+
+**A map** takes `image` and any of the other keys below. Any other key fails the build.
+
+| Key         | Required | What it sets                                                                    |
+| ----------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `image`     | yes      | The image reference.                                                            |
+| `name`      | no       | The container's name. Default: derived from the image, as for a string entry.   |
+| `resources` | no       | `requests` and `limits`, each a map of resource name → quantity.                |
+| `runAsUser` | no       | The container's `securityContext.runAsUser`.                                    |
+| `env`       | no       | Environment variables, name → value.                                            |
+
+```groovy
+yaml podYaml(templates: ['k8s'], images: [
+    [image: 'registry:5000/kube-coder-go-toolchain:latest', name: 'golang',
+        resources: [requests: [cpu: '2', memory: '2Gi'], limits: [cpu: '4', memory: '4Gi']]],
+    'node:24-bookworm',
+])
+```
+
+### Container names
+
+The name derived from a string entry is not checked against RFC 1123. Image repository names may
+hold `.` and `_`, which container names may not: `registry:5000/my_tool:1` derives `my_tool`.
+`podYaml` accepts it. The build then fails when the agent's pod template is parsed, before any pod
+is requested, with `Container Names MUST match RFC 1123 - They can only contain lowercase letters,
+numbers or dashes: my_tool`. An image whose last path segment is not a valid container name takes
+the map form, with an explicit `name:`.
+
+Two containers with the same name fail the build, whether they are two images or a template and an
+image.
+
+## Combining with inherited pod templates
+
+`inheritFrom` names the controller's pod templates the agent's pod builds on. An image build also
+inherits `kaniko`, whose `kaniko` container `helmCharts.kaniko2` runs in. The `kaniko` template is
+YAML only. Under the default YAML merge strategy the plugin keeps only the last YAML, which is this
+one, and drops the `kaniko` container with its `busybox-share-init` init container and its
+`busybox` volume. An agent that inherits `kaniko` therefore declares `yamlMergeStrategy merge()`:
+
+```groovy
+agent {
+    kubernetes {
+        inheritFrom 'jenkins-agent kaniko'
+        yamlMergeStrategy merge()
+        yaml podYaml(templates: ['k8s'])
+    }
+}
+```
+
+## Evaluated on the controller
+
+Declarative evaluates an agent's parameters on the controller, before any agent exists. `podYaml`
+and everything it calls is `@NonCPS` and runs no step, so the call works there.
+
+`sidecars`, `imageContainer`, `containerName`, `containerLines` and `quoted` are its internals.
+They are not part of what `podYaml` offers a Jenkinsfile.
+
+A scripted pipeline declares the same sidecars with [`containerTemplates`](containerTemplates.md).
