index 0000000..62db698
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/pages/guide/checkout.md
@@ -0,0 +1,65 @@
+# Checkout
+
+How a build gets its repos: the job's own, the others it reads, and the ones it pushes to.
+
+### CHK-1 — `skipDefaultCheckout()`, then a `Checkout` stage running `checkout scm` { #chk-1 }
+
+Every file MUST declare `skipDefaultCheckout()` in `options {}`. Its first stage MUST be
+`Checkout`, and that stage MUST check out the job's own repo with `checkout scm`. A file MUST NOT
+clone the job's own repo with `git`, or in a shell.
+
+**Why.**
+
+- Without the option, Declarative clones into the workspace root before the first stage, in a
+  stage the file does not name (`Declarative: Checkout SCM`). That clone cannot go into a `dir()`,
+  and a `checkout scm` of the file's own then clones a second time. With it, every build starts
+  with the same named stage.
+- `checkout scm` takes the repo, the branch and the credential from the job, so the branch is
+  written in one place. `GIT_COMMIT` and the build's change sets then come from the checkout the
+  job resolved.
+
+### CHK-2 — Other repos go beside the job's own { #chk-2 }
+
+When the build needs another repo beside its own:
+
+- `checkout scm` MUST run in `dir('<Repo>')`, the job's repo name as GitHub spells it;
+- each other repo MUST be cloned in the same `Checkout` stage, into `dir('<repo>')` named as GitHub
+  spells it, with `git url: …, branch: …, credentialsId: '5f6fbd66-b41c-405f-b107-85ba6fd97f10'`.
+
+**Why.** Every repo the build reads is in place before any build step runs, each under its own
+name. A clone inside a build stage hides a network step in a stage named for something else.
+
+### CHK-3 — A repo the job pushes to is cloned where it is pushed { #chk-3 }
+
+A repo the job pushes to MUST NOT be cloned in `Checkout`, and a push MUST NOT go from the
+`Checkout` stage's clone.
+
+- A pin write needs no clone: `cicd.writeVersionPins` clones the deploy repo itself.
+- Any other push clones the repo inside `withCredentials` ([SEC-3](secrets.md#sec-3)), in the
+  stage that pushes, and pushes from that clone. That holds for a push to the job's own repo too.
+
+**Why.** `checkout scm` and `git` hold the credential only while they fetch, so their clone has none
+to push with. The stage that pushes then holds the whole change, clone to push, and the credential
+exists only inside it.
+
+### CHK-4 — The iac-controller files too { #chk-4 }
+
+The iac-controller files MUST have the same `skipDefaultCheckout()` and `Checkout` stage.
+
+**Why.** Their `iac -c` calls clone the repo themselves, so no step reads the workspace checkout.
+It records the build's commit and its changes on the build page, and every file starts the same
+way.
+
+## Recipe
+
+A firmware build reads a second repo, `esp-libs`, so both go into a directory of their own:
+
+```groovy
+--8<-- "firmware.groovy:checkout"
+```
+
+A build that reads only its own repo checks it out at the workspace root:
+
+```groovy
+--8<-- "iac-controller.groovy:stages"
+```
