@@ -0,0 +1,114 @@
+# The library
+
+When code goes into JenkinsPipelineUtils, which of its calls a file uses, and where code that only
+one file uses goes.
+
+## When code goes into the library
+
+### LIB-1 — The contract test { #lib-1 }
+
+Code MUST go into the library when it carries a contract that must be the same across the estate:
+
+- how an image is built and labelled: `helmCharts.kaniko2`;
+- how a pin reaches a deploy repo: `cicd.writeVersionPins`;
+- how an alert reaches Telegram: `notify`;
+- which image a sidecar runs: `podYaml`'s templates;
+- how a whole pipeline type runs.
+
+Code that is one repo's own workflow MUST stay in that repo's files, however many copies of it
+there are.
+
+**Why.** A contract must change everywhere at once, and the library is the one place that
+reaches every file. A repo's own workflow is read with the file, and a helper would hide it from
+the reader of the file.
+
+### LIB-2 — Nothing the file should show { #lib-2 }
+
+The library MUST NOT take over what the file should show: the job's properties, its trigger, the
+size of its agent.
+
+**Why.** These are what a reader of the file needs to see first, and what [Job
+properties](job-properties.md) put in the file.
+
+### LIB-3 — A per-repo value is an argument with no default { #lib-3 }
+
+A value that differs per repo by design MUST be an argument of the library call, with no default.
+
+**Why.** Each file then states its own value, and a new file cannot inherit another repo's by
+leaving it out.
+
+### LIB-4 — A whole-pipeline helper needs three jobs of one body { #lib-4 }
+
+A helper that runs a whole pipeline type MUST be written only for a type with at least three jobs
+whose files are one body.
+
+**Why.** Below three, the helper costs more to keep than the copies it saves.
+
+### LIB-5 — A new var comes with its reference page { #lib-5 }
+
+A new var MUST come with its reference page, `vars/<name>.md`, in the same commit. The library's
+own test fails without it.
+
+**Why.** The page is how a Jenkinsfile's author learns what the var offers.
+
+**What a library change costs.** The library floats on `main` ([FILE-5](file-layout.md#file-5)),
+so a push to it changes every consumer at once, on each one's next build.
+
+### The estate's cases
+
+| Case | Test | Outcome |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| J14: `espFirmware(…)` for the eight ESP-IDF firmware jobs, with a required `idfVersion` | the type's whole pipeline ([LIB-1](#lib-1)); the ESP-IDF version per repo ([LIB-3](#lib-3)) | accepted, not yet in the library |
+| J16: `architectureProducer(…)` for the architecture producers, 23 app and 49 deploy-repo files | the type's whole pipeline | accepted, not yet in the library |
+| J21: one kaniko API, `helmCharts.kaniko2(…)` | how an image is built and labelled | in the library ([LIB-6](#lib-6)) |
+| J15: the validation-Job helper | the whole-pipeline fence ([LIB-4](#lib-4)): with the five apps it was for rendered from a template, it serves one job, SSEGateway | not built |
+| J19: an `iac` helper for the iac-controller dev stages | the iac-controller jobs' own workflow | ruled against: "Keep the duplication; the style guide says it is deliberate" ([LIB-7](#lib-7)) |
+| J01: a `jobDefaults()` var for the job properties | nothing the file should show ([LIB-2](#lib-2)) | ruled against: it "would hide exactly the lines the move exists to surface" |
+| A constant for the registry host, `registry:5000` | no contract: the host is the same in every image reference | ruled against: it would make the files "less readable to save nothing" |
+
+Until a type's helper is in the library, the type's reference file is the full declarative file.
+
+## The calls a file uses
+
+### LIB-6 — One kaniko API { #lib-6 }
+
+An image build MUST call `helmCharts.kaniko2(…)`, the map form. A file MUST NOT call the
+positional `helmCharts.kaniko(…)`.
+
+**Why.** One call for one contract. Only the map form takes `trackingTag`, `params`, `depends` and
+`rebuildDays` ([`helmCharts`](../reference/helmCharts.md)).
+
+In a declarative stage, a call on a var's method, such as `cicd.writeVersionPins(…)`, runs inside
+`script {}`; the linter refuses it outside one.
+
+### LIB-7 — The iac-controller files stay self-contained { #lib-7 }
+
+Each iac-controller file MUST carry its own copy of its dev-stage code: its `devUp()` probe and the
+dev-stage form of [POST-2](post-and-notify.md#post-2). No helper holds them, in the library or
+loaded from the repo.
+
+**Why.** The duplication is deliberate. Each file then describes everything its job does, in view,
+and the dev-stage code is the iac-controller jobs' own workflow ([LIB-1](#lib-1)).
+
+## Code local to one file
+
+### LIB-8 — A `def` before `pipeline {}` { #lib-8 }
+
+Logic that only one file uses MUST be a `def` in that file, after the library line and before
+`pipeline {}` ([FILE-6](file-layout.md#file-6)). It MUST be `@NonCPS` only when it is pure and
+calls no step.
+
+**Why.** A reader meets the helper before the pipeline that calls it. A step called from `@NonCPS`
+code fails, so only code that calls none can run outside the CPS interpreter.
+
+## Recipe
+
+A file-local check, placed between the library line and the pipeline, called from a `when {}`:
+
+```groovy
+--8<-- "change-detection.groovy:local"
+```
+
+```groovy
+--8<-- "change-detection.groovy:build"
+```
