@@ -0,0 +1,84 @@
+# Agent and pod
+
+Where a build runs: one pod per build, or the iac-controller node, and the containers in the pod.
+
+### POD-1 — One agent, at the top { #pod-1 }
+
+A pod pipeline MUST declare its agent once, at the top of `pipeline {}`, as
+`agent { kubernetes { … } }`. No stage declares an `agent`.
+
+**Why.** One pod per build is what every job does, and what the controller's cap of three agent
+pods is sized for. A stage agent is a second pod. A stage's `options {}` also run before the stage's
+agent is up, so a stage-level timeout would count the wait for it.
+
+### POD-2 — The iac-controller jobs run on `iac-controller` { #pod-2 }
+
+An iac-controller job MUST declare `agent { label 'iac-controller' }`.
+
+**Why.** Its steps are `iac` calls, which run on srviac, the controller's one `iac-controller`
+executor.
+
+### POD-3 — The inherited pod templates { #pod-3 }
+
+`inheritFrom` MUST name `jenkins-agent`, or `jenkins-agent-large` in the jobs that use it today:
+the eight ESP-IDF firmware jobs, Firmware/IntercomServer, IaC/HomelabTerraformProvider,
+MyDownloads/MyDownloads, MyDownloads/MyDownloadsClient, MyDownloads/MyDownloadsServer,
+ScanToPdf/ScanToPdf and ScanToPdf/ScanToPdfClient. A new job starts from its type's reference file,
+which names the template its type uses.
+
+It MUST add `kaniko` only when the build runs a kaniko step, and then MUST also declare
+`yamlMergeStrategy merge()`: `inheritFrom 'jenkins-agent kaniko'`.
+
+**Why.** The `kaniko` template is YAML only. Under the default YAML merge strategy, the Kubernetes
+plugin keeps only the last YAML, this file's, and drops the `kaniko` container
+([`podYaml`](../reference/podYaml.md#combining-with-inherited-pod-templates)). A build that runs no
+kaniko step does not need that container ([POD-6](#pod-6)).
+
+### POD-4 — Every other container from `podYaml`, each named { #pod-4 }
+
+Every container the pod adds MUST come from
+[`podYaml`](../reference/podYaml.md): `yaml podYaml(templates: [...], images: [...])`.
+
+- `templates:` names the library's sidecars ([POD-5](#pod-5)).
+- Every `images:` entry MUST be a map with an explicit `name:`, the name `container('<name>')`
+  uses: `[image: 'espressif/idf:v5.5.3', name: 'idf']`. An `images:` entry is never a string.
+
+**Why.** With `name:`, the container's name stands next to its image in the file. A name derived
+from the image can be one Kubernetes refuses, and the build then fails when the pod is created
+([`podYaml`](../reference/podYaml.md#container-names)).
+
+### POD-5 — A library sidecar comes from its template { #pod-5 }
+
+A container that runs one of the library's sidecar images MUST be named in `templates:`, never
+written out under `images:`. The sidecars are the ones
+[`containerTemplates`](../reference/containerTemplates.md) declares for scripted pipelines. A
+sidecar that `podYaml` has no template for yet gets its template in `podYaml`, as
+`containerTemplates` declares it, before a file uses it. `podYaml`'s page lists the templates it
+has.
+
+**Why.** Each sidecar image and its settings, such as its uid and environment, are then declared
+once, in the library. A new image tag reaches every file at once, and no file carries a copy that
+drifts.
+
+### POD-6 — No container that no step uses { #pod-6 }
+
+A pod MUST NOT declare a container, by template, image or inherited template, that no step of the
+file runs in.
+
+**Why.** Every container is pulled on every build, and holds its share of the pod's resources for
+the whole build.
+
+## Recipe
+
+An image build inherits `kaniko` for its kaniko step, and takes the `k8s` sidecar for its pin
+write:
+
+```groovy
+--8<-- "image-build.groovy:agent"
+```
+
+A firmware build on the large template, with the ESP-IDF image as a named container:
+
+```groovy
+--8<-- "firmware.groovy:agent"
+```
