@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@
+# Stage labels
+
+What a stage is called. The same work reads the same in every job's stage view, and a label says
+what its stage did. Each rule is a check on the label's string.
+
+### LABEL-1 — A verb, then its object { #label-1 }
+
+A label MUST be an imperative verb followed by its object, in sentence case: `Build firmware`, not
+`Building firmware`, `Firmware` or `Build Firmware`. A name in a label MUST be spelled as it is
+spelled elsewhere: an image as it is in the registry (`Build ginbov_nl image`), a job as it is in
+Jenkins (`Trigger MyDownloads`).
+
+**Why.** The verb says what the stage does, and a name spelled as elsewhere can be searched for.
+
+### LABEL-2 — The standard labels { #label-2 }
+
+A stage that does one of these MUST take its standard label:
+
+| Stage | Label |
+| --- | --- |
+| The checkout, always the first stage | `Checkout` |
+| Linters and format checks | `Lint` |
+| A test suite | `Test`, or `Test <component>` when there are several |
+| A validation of an artifact | `Validate <artifact>`, e.g. `Validate architecture` |
+| An image build | `Build <image> image`, e.g. `Build charts-home image` |
+| Any other build | `Build <artifact>`, e.g. `Build firmware`, `Build apk`, `Build provider` |
+| A generated file the job publishes | `Generate <artifact>`, e.g. `Generate architecture` |
+| The pin write | `Write image pins` |
+| Starting another job | `Trigger <job>`, e.g. `Trigger MyDownloads` |
+| An upload to devices | `Deploy firmware` |
+
+Any other stage picks its own imperative verb: `Apply configuration`, `Retag images`,
+`Push stable branch`.
+
+**Why.** The same work carries the same label in every job, so a stage view reads at a glance.
+
+### LABEL-3 — The scope goes last, in parentheses { #label-3 }
+
+A stage's scope or variant MUST go last, in parentheses: `(prd)`, `(k8s dev)`, `(v2)`, `(<tag>)`.
+In an iac-controller file: `Apply Terraform (prd)`, `Apply site-k8s (k8s dev)`,
+`Check drift (k8s prd)`.
+
+**Why.** The action reads the same across scopes, and the stages of one action line up.
+
+### LABEL-4 — No `+`; two actions are joined with `and` { #label-4 }
+
+A label MUST NOT contain `+`. A label that names two actions joins them with `and`: `Lint and test`,
+never `Lint + test`.
+
+**Why.** A label is read as words, and one joining form keeps labels uniform. Whether two actions
+share a stage at all is [GRAN-2](stage-granularity.md#gran-2)'s call.
+
+### LABEL-5 — Nothing that is not the stage { #label-5 }
+
+A label MUST NOT name the repo or the job, and MUST NOT name anything the stage does not do. A
+stage that only starts the MyDownloads job is `Trigger MyDownloads`, not `Build MyDownloads`.
+
+**Why.** The stage view already shows the job, and a label that names something else sends the
+reader of a red stage to the wrong place.
+
+### LABEL-6 — Unique and constant { #label-6 }
+
+A label MUST be unique within its file, and MUST be a string literal. Only the stages DockerImages
+generates compute their label ([GRAN-7](stage-granularity.md#gran-7)): `Build <image> image`, and
+`Build <image> image (<tag>)` for a variant of one image.
+
+**Why.** A fixed label is what the stage view, a search and a checker find the stage by.
+
+## Recipe
+
+An iac-controller job's labels: the standard `Checkout`, then one action with its two scopes.
+
+```groovy
+--8<-- "iac-controller.groovy:stages"
+```
