+# App architecture producer
+
+An app repo's `Jenkinsfile.architecture`, run by the job `AaC/<Repo>`. It validates the repo's
+hand-authored architecture model, `docs/architecture/*.yaml`, and archives it as the producer's
+artifact. AaC/Architecture copies the artifact from the job's last successful build.
+
+## What is specific to this type
+
+- **The `aac-tools` sidecar.** `arch-validate` runs in the container of `podYaml`'s `aac-tools`
+  template ([POD-5](../guide/pod.md#pod-5)), and submits the model to the architecture service.
+- **One stage after the checkout.** The model is committed, so the build makes nothing.
+  `Validate architecture` is the gate, and it archives the files it validated.
+- **The accepted helper.** J16's `architectureProducer(…)` is not in the library, so a producer's
+  file is this full file ([The library](../guide/library.md#the-estates-cases)).
+- **A new producer** also needs its entry in Architecture's `pipeline-producers.yaml`
+  ([A new repo](../guide/new-repo.md#recipe-the-steps), step 7).
+
+## The reference file
+
+The `AaC/Ginbov` job's `Jenkinsfile.architecture`:
+
+```groovy
+--8<-- "app-architecture.groovy"
+```
diff --git a/docs/pages/types/architecture-collector.md b/docs/pages/types/architecture-collector.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2c7f903
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/pages/types/architecture-collector.md
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+# Architecture collector
+
+AaC/Architecture collects the architecture model of every producer that Architecture's
+`pipeline-producers.yaml` registers, validates the federation with the collector, and builds the
+architecture viewer. It runs on a push to its repo, and whenever a registered producer's job
+succeeds.
+
+## What is specific to this type
+
+- **Computed triggers**, in the recipe below. The file has no `triggers {}`.
+- **`Collect producer artifacts`** copies each producer's artifact from its job's last successful
+  build, and archives them all as the collector's inputs.
+- **`abortPrevious: true`** ([PROP-3](../guide/job-properties.md#prop-3)): a newer build collects
+  every producer again.
+- **The `python` sidecar.** `podYaml` has no `python` template yet. By
+  [POD-5](../guide/pod.md#pod-5), it gets one, as `containerTemplates.python` declares it, before
+  a file names it. The linter does not evaluate the agent, so this file passes it.
+
+## Recipe: triggers computed from YAML
+
+The job's upstream triggers are the jobs of every registered producer, except its own and those
+marked `trigger: false`. `triggers {}` is fixed when the file is parsed and cannot hold a list read
+at run time. So:
+
+- **A `Set triggers` stage**, right after `Checkout`, reads `pipeline-producers.yaml` and sets
+  `githubPush()` and one `upstream` trigger with `properties([pipelineTriggers([...])])`. It is the
+  one `properties` step in the estate ([PROP-8](../guide/job-properties.md#prop-8)).
+- **`options {}` still declares the concurrency.** Declarative leaves alone the triggers its
+  `triggers {}` did not declare, so each build keeps the ones the previous build set, and the
+  build of the commit that registers a producer wires its trigger.
+
+```groovy
+--8<-- "architecture-collector.groovy:triggers"
+```
+
+**Why not the alternatives.** A literal `triggers { upstream(…) }` kept equal to
+`pipeline-producers.yaml` by a check makes every registration two edits. Having each producer
+start AaC/Architecture itself puts the same line into every producer's file.
+
+## The reference file
+
+The `AaC/Architecture` job's `Jenkinsfile`:
+
+```groovy
+--8<-- "architecture-collector.groovy"
+```
