+# Configuration apply
+
+A repo that holds a live service's configuration as code: every push lints it, tests it and
+applies it to the service. Today this is YouTrack/YouTrackConfiguration.
+
+## What is specific to this type
+
+- **The gates come first**: `Lint`, then `Test`, each a stage of its own
+  ([GRAN-2](../guide/stage-granularity.md#gran-2)). Syncing the dependencies is part of the first
+  stage that needs them ([GRAN-5](../guide/stage-granularity.md#gran-5)).
+- **The apply is the change outside the build**, last
+  ([GRAN-6](../guide/stage-granularity.md#gran-6)), and the only step that holds the service's
+  token ([SEC-1](../guide/secrets.md#sec-1)).
+- **Plain `disableConcurrentBuilds()` and the abort marker**: an apply to a live system
+  ([PROP-3](../guide/job-properties.md#prop-3)).
+- **The `python` sidecar.** `podYaml` has no `python` template yet. By
+  [POD-5](../guide/pod.md#pod-5), it gets one, as `containerTemplates.python` declares it, before
+  a file names it. The linter does not evaluate the agent, so this file passes it.
+
+## The reference file
+
+The `YouTrack/YouTrackConfiguration` job's `Jenkinsfile`:
+
+```groovy
+--8<-- "configuration-apply.groovy"
+```
