+# ESP-IDF firmware
+
+A device's firmware build: it builds the firmware with ESP-IDF and uploads it to the devices over
+the air, through IoTSupport. Today these are the eight jobs
+[PROP-3](../guide/job-properties.md#prop-3) lists.
+
+## What is specific to this type
+
+- **The `jenkins-agent-large` template** ([POD-3](../guide/pod.md#pod-3)), and the ESP-IDF image
+  as a named `images:` entry ([POD-4](../guide/pod.md#pod-4)).
+- **`esp-libs` beside the repo**, both cloned in `Checkout`, each in its own directory
+  ([CHK-2](../guide/checkout.md#chk-2)). A repo that needs another library clones it there too.
+- **The upload holds the secret.** `Deploy firmware` reads the IoTSupport client secret with
+  `withVault` around the upload alone ([SEC-1](../guide/secrets.md#sec-1)).
+- **Plain `disableConcurrentBuilds()` and the abort marker**: an upload cut off by an abort leaves
+  the devices on two firmware versions ([PROP-3](../guide/job-properties.md#prop-3)).
+- **The accepted helper.** J14's `espFirmware(…)`, with its required `idfVersion`, is not in the
+  library, so a firmware file is this full file
+  ([The library](../guide/library.md#the-estates-cases)).
+
+## The reference file
+
+The `Firmware/PaperClock` job's `Jenkinsfile`:
+
+```groovy
+--8<-- "firmware.groovy"
+```
+
+## Several hardware versions
+
+Intercom builds its firmware for two hardware versions, and writes out a Build and Deploy pair for
+each ([GRAN-7](../guide/stage-granularity.md#gran-7)): the list is a constant of the file, and every
+stage is linted. The version is the stage's scope, last and in parentheses
+([LABEL-3](../guide/stage-labels.md#label-3)).
+
+The order is build, deploy, build, deploy. Both versions build into the one `build/` directory, so
+building the second version before the first is deployed would overwrite the first's image.
+
+The `Firmware/Intercom` job's `Jenkinsfile`:
+
+```groovy
+--8<-- "firmware-versions.groovy"
+```
