+# iac-controller job
+
+A job of the Ansible repo that runs on srviac, the controller's one `iac-controller` executor.
+Every step is an `iac -c '…'` call. Today these are IaC/Build-Main (lint, validate and plan on a
+push), IaC/Apply (started by hand) and the four `IaC/Scheduled …` jobs, each running one of the
+repo's `Jenkinsfile.iac-*` files.
+
+## What is specific to this type
+
+- **`agent { label 'iac-controller' }`** ([POD-2](../guide/pod.md#pod-2)). Each `iac -c` call
+  clones the repo itself, and the `Checkout` stage still runs
+  ([CHK-4](../guide/checkout.md#chk-4)).
+- **A 4-hour backstop** ([TIME-2](../guide/timeouts.md#time-2)), **plain
+  `disableConcurrentBuilds()` and the abort marker** ([PROP-3](../guide/job-properties.md#prop-3)).
+- **The trigger follows the job**: `githubPush()` for IaC/Build-Main, a `cron` for a scheduled
+  job, none for IaC/Apply ([PROP-6](../guide/job-properties.md#prop-6)).
+- **A stage per target, prd and dev apart**, the scope last in the label:
+  `Restart calico-node (k8s prd)` ([LABEL-3](../guide/stage-labels.md#label-3)).
+- **The dev stages**: a `devUp()` probe, the playbook bounded in the shell
+  ([TIME-5](../guide/timeouts.md#time-5)), and a failure that warns, then marks the build unstable
+  ([POST-2](../guide/post-and-notify.md#post-2)). Each file carries its own copy
+  ([LIB-7](../guide/library.md#lib-7)).
+
+## The reference file
+
+The `IaC/Scheduled Calico Rollout` job's `Jenkinsfile.iac-scheduled-calico`:
+
+```groovy
+--8<-- "iac-controller.groovy"
+```
