+# Image build
+
+An app's build: it builds the app's image with kaniko, pushes it to `registry:5000`, and pins it
+into the app's deploy repo, which Argo CD syncs. Some builds test, compile or copy another job's
+artifact first; a few build an image that no deploy repo pins.
+
+## What is specific to this type
+
+- **The `kaniko` template**, inherited with `yamlMergeStrategy merge()`
+  ([POD-3](../guide/pod.md#pod-3)), and the `k8s` sidecar for the pin write.
+- **A stage per image** ([GRAN-3](../guide/stage-granularity.md#gran-3)), labelled
+  `Build <image> image` with the image's registry name ([LABEL-2](../guide/stage-labels.md#label-2)).
+  A lint or a test before it is a stage of its own ([GRAN-2](../guide/stage-granularity.md#gran-2)).
+  Copying another job's artifact into the image's context is part of the image's stage
+  ([GRAN-5](../guide/stage-granularity.md#gran-5)).
+- **`Write image pins` last**, one stage for every pin of the build
+  ([GRAN-4](../guide/stage-granularity.md#gran-4)). A build whose image no deploy repo pins ends
+  with its image stage and has no `k8s` container ([POD-6](../guide/pod.md#pod-6)).
+- **A build that detects its changes** builds its image only when the push changed what the image
+  is built from, or the `image` parameter names it. It declares plain `disableConcurrentBuilds()`
+  and carries the abort marker ([PROP-3](../guide/job-properties.md#prop-3)).
+
+## The reference files
+
+The `Ginbov` job's `Jenkinsfile`:
+
+```groovy
+--8<-- "image-build.groovy"
+```
+
+A build that detects its changes, and pins nothing: the `IaC/IaC Docker Image` job's
+`Jenkinsfile.iac-image`.
+
+```groovy
+--8<-- "change-detection.groovy"
+```
