@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+# Image matrix
+
+DockerImages builds many images, and every variant of an image gets a stage of its own. The
+variants are listed at run time, from the image folders, by `tools/collect-internal-dependencies.py`.
+A build builds the images the push changed, every image built on top of one, and those its `image`
+parameter names; `image=all` builds every image.
+
+## What is specific to this type
+
+- **The stage generator** below: the one file whose stages are not all written out
+  ([GRAN-7](../guide/stage-granularity.md#gran-7)).
+- **180 minutes**, the one exception to the standard timeout
+  ([TIME-3](../guide/timeouts.md#time-3)).
+- **Plain `disableConcurrentBuilds()` and the abort marker**: the build decides from its change
+  sets what to build ([PROP-3](../guide/job-properties.md#prop-3)).
+- **The `python` sidecar.** `podYaml` has no `python` template yet. By
+  [POD-5](../guide/pod.md#pod-5), it gets one, as `containerTemplates.python` declares it, before
+  a file names it. The linter does not evaluate the agent, so this file passes it.
+
+## Recipe: a stage per image variant
+
+Declarative fixes a file's stages when it parses the file, and the variants are known only once
+the checkout is there. So:
+
+- **One declarative stage, `Build images`**, lists the variants and works out which images to
+  build. It then runs a nested `stage('Build <image> image')` for each variant, with `(<tag>)`
+  added for a variant of one image ([LABEL-6](../guide/stage-labels.md#label-6)).
+- **An image it does not build** is marked skipped with `Utils.markStageSkippedForConditional`
+  ([GRAN-8](../guide/stage-granularity.md#gran-8)), which needs the file's one import
+  ([FILE-6](../guide/file-layout.md#file-6)).
+- **`Write image pins` is an ordinary stage**, with `when {}`. The tags the images were pushed
+  with reach it in variables declared before `pipeline {}`.
+
+```groovy
+--8<-- "image-matrix.groovy:generator"
+```
+
+**Why not a `matrix`.** A `matrix` needs its axis values written in the file, a list that
+duplicates the image folders. It runs its cells in parallel, and every image would then build at
+once in the one pod.
+
+## The reference file
+
+The `DockerImages` job's `Jenkinsfile`:
+
+```groovy
+--8<-- "image-matrix.groovy"
+```
