+# Promotion
+
+A job started by hand that moves a validated commit of a deploy repo to prd: it retags the images
+the commit pins, fast-forwards the `prd` branch, and tags the release. Today this is
+KubeCoder/Promote-PRD.
+
+## What is specific to this type
+
+- **Started by hand**: no `triggers {}` ([PROP-6](../guide/job-properties.md#prop-6)); the commit
+  to promote is a parameter ([PROP-7](../guide/job-properties.md#prop-7)).
+- **`Validate commit` reads the `Checkout` stage's clone.** `checkout scm` fetches every branch
+  and tag of the repo, so the gate needs no clone of its own. What it resolves reaches the later
+  stages in variables declared before `pipeline {}`.
+- **`Retag images` retags every pinned image in one stage**
+  ([GRAN-4](../guide/stage-granularity.md#gran-4)).
+- **Each push is a stage of its own**, from a clone made inside `withCredentials`:
+  `Advance prd` and `Tag release` ([CHK-3](../guide/checkout.md#chk-3)).
+- **A re-run that only records the release** skips the retag and the `prd` push with `when {}`
+  ([GRAN-8](../guide/stage-granularity.md#gran-8)).
+- **Plain `disableConcurrentBuilds()` and the abort marker**: a sequence of changes an abort would
+  cut in half ([PROP-3](../guide/job-properties.md#prop-3)).
+
+## The reference file
+
+The `KubeCoder/Promote-PRD` job's `Jenkinsfile.promote`, in the KubeCoderDeploy repo:
+
+```groovy
+--8<-- "promotion.groovy"
+```
